<div class="note" style="margin-bottom:16px">
  Master data is held as rows, not code. When the tender is revised — a new manpower band, a changed penalty rate —
  these tables change and nothing is redeployed.
</div>
<div class="grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(280px,1fr))">
  <% [
    ['/masters/designations','Designations','Schedule-A roles, skill category, qualification requirement and the per-role floor used when scaling'],
    ['/masters/manpower-norms','Manpower norms','The Schedule-A matrix: one staff table each for 50 / 100 / 150 / 200 / 250 beds'],
    ['/masters/deficiency-clauses','Deficiency schedule','All 50 clauses from the tender annexure. Rates are stored but not applied in this build'],
    ['/masters/vendors','Washing centres & operators','Approval, the periodic premises inspection and withdrawal — clause C1 turns on this being current'],
    ['/masters/menu','Menu card & rate board','Schedule-B Table A and Table B. The tender fixes no rate for the optional items — clause B6 has nothing to test until the Railway does']
  ].forEach(function(m){ %>
  <a class="card" href="<%= url(m[0]) %>" style="text-decoration:none;color:inherit">
    <div class="card-b">
      <div style="font-size:14px;font-weight:650;margin-bottom:4px"><%= m[1] %></div>
      <div class="muted" style="font-size:12px"><%= m[2] %></div>
    </div>
  </a>
  <% }); %>
</div>
